Title: Introduction to Differentiation
Content:
Definition of Derivative
The derivative of a function measures how the function changes as its input changes.
Power Rule
If f(x) = x^n, then f'(x) = n*x^(n-1)
Product Rule
If f(x) = u(x)v(x), then
f'(x) = u'(x)v(x) + u(x)v'(x)
Chain Rule
If f(x) = g(h(x)), then
f'(x) = g'(h(x)) * h'(x)
Applications
Derivatives are used to:
Compute slopes of tangent lines
Solve optimization problems
Model rates of change
